# Descent, Lemma 05VG: local generation by sections, site by site

Let `S` be a scheme and `𝓕` a quasi-coherent `𝒪_S`-module.  Descent, Lemma 05VG says that `𝓕`
has a property `𝒫` of Modules on Sites, Definitions 03DE, 03DL, 03ER if and only if the module
`𝓕^a` of Descent, Proposition 03DX has `𝒫` as an `𝒪`-module, on the big site `(Sch/S)_τ` and on
the small site `S_τ`, for each `τ ∈ {Zariski, étale, smooth, syntomic, fppf}`.  This file states
that equivalence for `𝒫` = **locally generated by sections**, Modules on Sites, Definition
03DL (3), once for each of the ten sites, with the predicate
`SheafOfModules.IsLocallyGeneratedBySectionsOnSite` on both sides: on `S` it is read on the
ringed site of opens of `S`, on the other side on the site in question with its structure sheaf.

Both sides hold for a quasi-coherent module: quasi-coherent data supplies, over each member of
a covering of the final object, a presentation whose generators are generating sections
(Definition 03DL (6) ⟹ 03DL (3)), and `𝓕^a` is quasi-coherent on every one of the ten sites
(Descent, Lemma 03DV).

## Main results

The ten cells of the row, each a separate theorem in `AlgebraicGeometry.Cells05VG`:

* big site `(Sch/S)_Zar`: `isLocallyGeneratedBySectionsOnSite_iff_baseAssociatedModule_zariski`
* big site `(Sch/S)_étale`: `isLocallyGeneratedBySectionsOnSite_iff_baseAssociatedModule_etale`
* big site `(Sch/S)_smooth`: `isLocallyGeneratedBySectionsOnSite_iff_baseAssociatedModule_smooth`
* big site `(Sch/S)_syntomic`:
  `isLocallyGeneratedBySectionsOnSite_iff_baseAssociatedModule_syntomic`
* big site `(Sch/S)_fppf`: `isLocallyGeneratedBySectionsOnSite_iff_baseAssociatedModule_fppf`
* small site `S_Zar`: `isLocallyGeneratedBySectionsOnSite_iff_smallZariskiAssociatedModule`
* small site `S_étale`: `isLocallyGeneratedBySectionsOnSite_iff_smallEtaleAssociatedModule`
* small site `S_smooth`:
  `isLocallyGeneratedBySectionsOnSite_iff_smallFlatSiteAssociatedModule_smooth`
* small site `S_syntomic`:
  `isLocallyGeneratedBySectionsOnSite_iff_smallFlatSiteAssociatedModule_syntomic`
* small site `S_fppf`: `isLocallyGeneratedBySectionsOnSite_iff_smallFlatSiteAssociatedModule_fppf`

## Implementation notes

The big sites are `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.baseAssociatedModule B S hS τ` at the five
constructors of `SiteKind`; the small Zariski and étale sites are
`AlgebraicGeometry.SmallZariski.associatedModule` and
`AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.associatedModule`; the small smooth, syntomic and fppf sites are
`AlgebraicGeometry.SmallFlatSite.associatedModule`
at the three constructors of `FlatSiteKind`.  Each cell specialises the corresponding uniform
statement:
`AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.isLocallyGeneratedBySectionsOnSite_baseAssociatedModule_iff`,
`AlgebraicGeometry.SmallZariski.isLocallyGeneratedBySectionsOnSite_associatedModule_iff`,
`AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.isLocallyGeneratedBySectionsOnSite_associatedModule_iff` and
`AlgebraicGeometry.SmallFlatSite.isLocallyGeneratedBySectionsOnSite_iff_associatedModule`.
The only hypothesis is the source's, quasi-coherence of `𝓕`.

